This folder holds what ARTS keeps of Evans' PolRadTran radiative transfer
models RT3 and RT4: the licence and description of the package, and his
benchmark scripts and data, which ARTS's tests read.

Origin: PolRadTran.tar from https://nit.coloradolinux.com/polrad.html
(sha256 7b0eff794319330321e27a6f312588a289ed080bb266500dcecf485f6a7cff9d),
under the MIT licence in LICENSE, which must be kept with the code: ARTS's
RT3 and RT4 (src/core/polradtran) are C++ ports of the tar's Fortran, with
ARTS's changes (doc/arts/dev.rt3.rst and doc/arts/dev.rt4.rst).  README is
Evans' description of the package.  RT3 (randomly oriented particles,
solar and thermal sources, all Fourier azimuth modes, I, Q, U and V) is
Evans and Stephens (1991), JQSRT 46, 413-423; RT4 (horizontally oriented
particles, thermal source, I and Q) is Evans and Stephens (1995), J. Atmos.
Sci. 52, 2058-2072.

Kept from the tar, unchanged: LICENSE, README, Evans' four benchmark scripts
runmietest, runtesta (RT3), runtestr and runtestc (RT4), which define their
problems and hold his expected outputs, and cl340d14.dda, the RT4
scattering file that runtestc reads.  They are read by cpp.fast.rt3-test,
cpp.fast.vdisort-rt3-test and cpp.fast.polradtran-rt4-arts (through
src/tests/polradtran/evans-scripts.h) and by
tests/core/disort/evans-benchmarks.rt3.rt4.py.

The Fortran (rt3.f, rt4.f, scatcnv.f and the rad*.f subroutines, with the
ARTS 2 and ARTS 3 changes to them, and the C interfaces to them) was removed
once the port was complete, as the C++ calls none of it.  Its outputs for
the cases of cpp.fast.rt3-radtran-test and cpp.fast.rt4-radtrano-test are
kept as the references of those tests (rt3-radtran-reference.h and
rt4-radtrano-reference.h).  The ARTS changes to the Fortran are listed in
the history of this file.
